`,s.jsxs(v,{title:"Where IoU is blind",children:[s.jsxs(e.p,{children:[s.jsx(e.strong,{children:"It saturates at 0."})," Two boxes that do not touch score 0 whether they are 5 or 500 pixels apart, so IoU used ",s.jsx(e.em,{children:"as a loss"}),' has zero gradient exactly where you most need one. GIoU adds a penalty for the empty space in the smallest enclosing box, restoring a signal — drag to "miss" in the widget and watch GIoU keep falling while IoU flatlines.']}),s.jsxs(e.p,{children:[s.jsx(e.strong,{children:"It ignores aspect ratio and centre offset separately."})," Two very different errors can produce the same IoU. DIoU and CIoU add explicit centre-distance and aspect-ratio terms for that reason."]})]}),`
